---@class posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchTileLayoutBoxOpenApi
---@field x number Column position in the dashboard grid (0-indexed).
---@field y number Row position in the dashboard grid (0-indexed).
---@field w number Width in grid columns. The desktop grid is 12 columns wide.
---@field h number Height in grid rows.

---@class posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchTileLayoutsOpenApi
---@field sm posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchTileLayoutBoxOpenApi Layout for the standard (desktop) breakpoint. The grid is 12 columns wide. A write replaces the tile's whole layout and the dashboard reads desktop placement from this box, so send it whenever you send layouts.
---@field xs? posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchTileLayoutBoxOpenApi Layout for the small (mobile) breakpoint, on a 1-column grid. The dashboard derives this layout from the sm order and heights, so a stored xs box does not change what renders.

---@class posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchTileOpenApi
---@field id? number Dashboard tile ID to update.
---@field layouts? posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchTileLayoutsOpenApi Grid position and size per breakpoint. Works for every tile type, including insight tiles. A write replaces the tile's whole layout, so send a complete sm box rather than the one value you want to change. Boxes are stored as sent and overlaps are not resolved, so send sm boxes that do not overlap, and include every tile you move in the same request.
---@field show_description? boolean Whether to show the tile's description underneath its title on the dashboard. Works for every tile type. The description itself is unaffected and still comes from the tile's insight, text, or widget content — this only toggles whether it renders on the dashboard.
---@field group_key? string|distilled.Null Key that puts this tile in a group with the other tiles that have the same key on this dashboard. Set the group's title and style in the dashboard's groups. Null or an empty string removes the tile from its group.
---@field badge? posthog.dashboards.DashboardTileBadgeEnum|string|distilled.Null Badge on the tile. winner shows a crown in the top left corner, for example to mark the best tile in a group. cheeky-hog shows a hedgehog when a person hovers over the tile. Null removes the badge. More than one tile in a group can have the winner badge. * `winner` - Winner * `cheeky-hog` - Cheeky hog
---@field widget? posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchWidgetOpenApi Nested widget row updates.

---@class posthog.dashboards.DashboardPatchWidgetOpenApi
---@field id? string Existing widget row ID when updating a widget tile via dashboard PATCH.
---@field widget_type? posthog.dashboards.DashboardWidgetTypeEnum|string Widget type identifier (cannot be changed on update). * `activity_events_list` - Activity Events List * `canvas_app` - Canvas App * `conversations_recent_tickets` - Conversations Recent Tickets * `error_tracking_list` - Error Tracking List * `experiment_results` - Experiment Results * `experiments_list` - Experiments List * `logs_list` - Logs List * `metrics_table` - Metrics Table * `notebook_widget` - Notebook Widget * `session_replay_list` - Session Replay List * `survey_results` - Survey Results
---@field config? posthog.dashboards.DashboardWidgetConfig Widget-specific configuration. Shape depends on the tile's widget_type.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null Optional custom display name for the widget tile.
---@field description? string Optional markdown description shown when show_description is enabled.

