---@class posthog.dashboards.ListDashboardsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field created_by? string Optional. Return only dashboards created by the user with this UUID.
---@field exclude_generated? boolean Optional. Exclude dashboards that PostHog generated.
---@field folder? string Optional. Return only dashboards filed directly in this project-tree folder, e.g. 'Unfiled/Dashboards'. An empty string matches dashboards at the project root. Nested sub-folders are not included.
---@field format? posthog.dashboards.ListDashboardsRequestFormat|string
---@field limit? number Number of results to return per page.
---@field offset? number The initial index from which to return the results.
---@field ordering? posthog.dashboards.ListDashboardsRequestOrdering|string Optional. `-last_viewed_at` puts the dashboards you viewed most recently first. A dashboard you never viewed sorts by its creation time. This order replaces the search relevance order.
---@field pinned? boolean Optional. Return only pinned dashboards.
---@field search? string Optional. Match against dashboard `name`, `description`, and tag names. Returns exact (case-insensitive substring) matches only; if no exact match exists, returns similar (fuzzy trigram — typos, transpositions, prefix-as-you-type) matches instead. Results are then ordered by relevance, then pinned status, then name; each result's `search_match_type` is `exact` or `similar`. When omitted, dashboards are ordered by pinned status then alphabetical name. Capped at 200 characters; longer queries return a 400 error.

---@alias posthog.dashboards.ListDashboardsRequestFormat "json"|"txt"

---@alias posthog.dashboards.ListDashboardsRequestOrdering "-last_viewed_at"

